  "interpretive_limits": [
    "Within declared original Model3 reproduction, the viable-self term dominates the exact assurance allele expected-direction response to a two-parent heterozygosity edit at fixed assurance high-copy count. The outcross mother marginal generally offsets it.",
    "The matched parent allele count does NOT guarantee fixed offspring seed intensity, source selfing fraction, maternal/census distributions or genomic background associations of the two edited individuals.",
    "At budget8 capped expected recruits remain exactly at the K=32 ceiling for all evaluated late assay paths; this is an engineered saturated regime, not evidence that biological recruitment is unaffected by assurance genotype.",
    "At budget3 observed mean capped recruitment differences are small relative to their nested-demographic Monte Carlo SE; cannot reliably rank demographic risk effects.",
    "HET_UP and HET_DOWN operate on DIFFERENT feasibility subsets at late fixation and cannot be combined without a common-support qualification.",
    "All edited parental states are hypothetical, not generated by original no-mutation, no-immigration evolution. They preserve allele copies but change two individual assurance genotype pairings relative to a shuffled sham.",
    "One archived old visitor history with nested demographic simulations, no independently confirmed ecological conditions, natural plant data or validated continuous-time SDE/SPDE."
